response:
A holographic will in Italy must be:

* written entirely by the testator’s own hand;  
* dated with the day, month and year;  
* signed by the testator, with the signature placed at the end of the provisions.  

Even if the signature does not contain the testator’s full name, the will is still valid provided it clearly identifies the testator. [S1]

